{{Quote|You and the Naboo form a symbiont circle. What happens to one of you will affect the other. You must understand this.|[[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], to [[Rugor Nass]]|<ref name="TPM" />}}
The '''Naboo''' (singular "Naboo"), also known as '''Naboolians'''<ref name="Bane">{{StoryCite|story=Bane's Story|book=The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark}}</ref> or '''Nabooians''',<ref name="Shadow Warrior">{{TCW|Shadow Warrior}}</ref> were a cultural group of [[human]]s from the [[planet]] [[Naboo]].<ref name="TPM" /> Contrary to the [[Homeworld|native]] [[Gungan]]s, with whom they shared their world, the Naboo originated offworld as human [[colonist]]s from [[Grizmallt]].<ref name="Crisis">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/crisis-on-naboo-trivia-gallery|text="Crisis on Naboo" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|slides 2-3 captions}}</ref> The Naboo [[Noble|aristocrats]] were known for their [[Clothing|sartorial]] extravagance.<ref name="Tark">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> Unlike the Gungans, who were a proud warrior [[species]], the human colonists of Naboo were peaceful. This contrast of ideology caused tension between the two civilizations for [[Standard century|centuries]].<ref name="SWE Gungan Grand Army">{{SWE|groups|gungangrandarmy|Gungan Grand Army}}</ref>

==Society and culture==
The Naboo valued culture and beauty, which was reflected in their everyday [[Clothing|attire]]. [[Youngling|Children]] wore graceful clothes made of natural materials.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

==History==
===Before the Invasion===
The Naboo originated as a group of [[human]] colonists who fled the [[Grizmallti civil war|war-torn]] [[Core Worlds|Core World]] of [[Grizmallt]] thousands of [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> Led by [[Kwilaan]], the colonists crashed on the [[homeworld]] of the [[Gungan]] species and established their presence there. They ventured into the [[Gallo Mountains]] and created a [[farm]]ing community at [[Dee'ja Peak]].<ref name="Crisis" /> At first, the Gungans tried to avoid contact with the colonists, retreating in the planet's waterways. When the humans and Gungans finally met, however, their relations soon turned to hostility<ref name="Rise" /> in the [[Human-Gungan conflicts|Grizmallti–Gungan wars]].<ref name="Nexus">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref> After fighting over territory and resources for a long time, the two species eventually resolved to simply live apart and ignore each other.<ref name="Rise" />

Following the end of their conflicts with the Gungans, the Naboo had to deal with internal wars, as their various city-states broke into factions and engaged in open warfare<ref name="Rise" /> in what was remembered as the [[Time of Suffering]].<ref name="Nexus" /> Eventually, each side became unified in its own way,<ref name="Rise" /> although [[General]]-<ref name="Nexus" />-turned-[[King]] [[Jafan]] also played a role.<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> The end of the fighting end brought about a [[Great Time of Peace]].<ref name="Nexus" /> Generations before [[32 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines 32 note">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' establishes that the events of ''[[Queen's Peril]]'' occur in [[32 BBY]]. Furthermore, ''Queen's Peril'' establishes that the [[Gungan-Naboo dispute]] was "generations" prior, putting it "generations" before 32 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].</ref> a [[Gungan-Naboo dispute|dispute]] arose between the Gungans and Naboo, during which the [[Monarch of Naboo]] needed the company of [[bodyguard]]s.<ref name="Queen's Peril">''[[Queen's Peril]]''</ref>

===The Naboo Crisis===
In [[32 BBY]], the [[Trade Federation]] [[Invasion of Naboo|blockaded and invaded]] Naboo. The [[Monarch of Naboo|Queen]], [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], was forced to flee the planet with [[Jedi]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]; she later returned to Naboo to help her people, and [[Boss Meetup|requested]] the help of [[Rugor Nass|Boss Nass]] and the Gungans.<ref name="TPM" />

Eventually, the combined forces of the two Jedi were able to defeat the Federation and the [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul|Darth Maul]], at the cost of the lives of Qui-Gon Jinn and many Gungans and Naboo.<ref name="TPM" /> The Naboo Crisis was the prelude to a much larger conflict, as the Trade Federation would eventually join with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] in the Clone Wars.<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref>

